.Dd December 21, 2026
.Dt ICOWM-THEME 5
.Os icowm-1.0.1
.Sh NAME
.Nm themes/name.json
.Nd theme file format for IcoWM
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A theme file describes the appearance of everything
.Xr icowm 1
draws: window frames and titlebars, desktop icons, the menus, the
dialogs, the system tray, the search box and the prompt.
.Pp
Themes live under
.Pa themes/
in the configuration directory, one file each, and the one to load is
named by
.Ic theme
in
.Xr icowm 5 ,
without the
.Ql .json
suffix.
Every key is optional: what a file leaves out keeps the built-in
default, so a theme need only state what it changes.
.Pp
.Ic name
at the top level is the theme's own name, reported in the window
information dialog.
A key beginning with
.Ql -
or
.Ql _
is ignored, which is how
.Ic -author ,
.Ic -creation-date
and the like are written as comments.
.Ss Common shapes
Several shapes recur throughout, and are described once here:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic color
An object with
.Ic background
and
.Ic foreground ,
each an
.Ql #RRGGBB
string.
.It Ic border
An object with
.Ic color ,
an
.Ql #RRGGBB
string, and
.Ic width ,
in pixels.
.It Ic padding
An object with
.Ic horizontal
and
.Ic vertical ,
in pixels.
.It Ic font
A string; see
.Sx Fonts
below.
.It Ic opacity
An integer from 0 to 100.
.Pp
Opacity is published on the window through
.Ql _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY
and nothing more.
.Xr icowm 1
never composites anything itself, so any value other than 100 has no
visible effect whatever unless a compositing manager, such as
.Xr picom 1 ,
is also running and reading the property back.
Without one, a theme may set this freely and nothing on screen will
change.
.El
.Ss Sections
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic window
The frame around an ordinary window.
.Ic active
and
.Ic inactive
each hold a
.Ic color ,
a
.Ic border ,
a
.Ic font
and an
.Ic opacity ,
for the focused window and the rest.
.Ic titlebar
holds its
.Ic height ,
its text
.Ic alignment ,
its
.Ic padding ,
and a
.Ic buttons
object naming which buttons sit
.Ic left
and which
.Ic right ,
with a
.Ic color
having
.Ic on
and
.Ic off
for pressed and idle.
.Ic is-decorated
decides whether a window is framed at all by default.
.It Ic icon
A desktop icon, in the same
.Ic active
and
.Ic inactive
shape.
.Ic is-captioned
decides whether the window name is shown beneath it, and
.Ic show-hints
and
.Ic show-pixmaps
whether the icon comes from the window's own hints and pixmaps.
.It Ic cycle
The frame drawn around the window being cycled to, through
.Ic border .
.It Ic systray
The tray's own
.Ic color ,
.Ic border ,
.Ic font ,
.Ic opacity
and
.Ic height ,
plus
.Ic pixmap
with the
.Ic size
of a docked icon and the
.Ic padding
around it, and
.Ic text
with the
.Ic gap
before the clock and its vertical
.Ic valign .
.It Ic desktop
The desktop background, through
.Ic color .
.It Ic menu
.Ic unselected ,
.Ic selected
and
.Ic label
each hold a
.Ic color ,
a
.Ic border
and a
.Ic font ,
for an ordinary row, the one under the pointer, and a heading.
.Ic disabled
holds the
.Ic color
of a row that cannot be chosen,
.Ic separator
the
.Ic color
of a dividing line, and the section itself a
.Ic border ,
a
.Ic padding ,
an
.Ic opacity
and
.Ic show-pixmaps .
.It Ic dialog
.Ic color
and
.Ic border
for the dialog itself,
.Ic label
for its text, and
.Ic button
holding the
.Ic gap
between buttons, their
.Ic padding ,
and a
.Ic selected
and
.Ic unselected
style each.
.It Ic overlay
The small box reporting a geometry during a drag, through
.Ic color ,
.Ic border ,
.Ic font
and
.Ic opacity .
.It Ic search
The window search box:
.Ic input
for the field,
.Ic selected
and
.Ic unselected
for its rows, and a
.Ic border .
.It Ic prompt
The command box:
.Ic label ,
.Ic input
and a
.Ic border .
.It Ic scratchpad
The scratchpad window's own
.Ic border .
.It Ic xsettings
What is published to XSettings-aware toolkits:
.Ic is-enabled ,
a
.Ic dpi ,
and a
.Ic theme
object naming
.Ic gtk-theme-name ,
.Ic icon-theme-name ,
.Ic cursor-theme-name
and
.Ic cursor-theme-size .
This changes nothing about what
.Xr icowm 1
itself draws; it only tells other applications what to use.
.El
.Ss Fonts
Every
.Ic font
field takes the same kind of string, tried through two backends in
order.
.Pp
X core fonts are tried first, through XCB.
Only X11 bitmap fonts, BDF and PCF, are reachable this way; it goes
first because it costs nothing per glyph and every X server ships the
.Ql fixed
family.
A short description such as
.Ql \&"fixed bold 13\&"
almost always takes this path.
.Pp
Anything that does not resolve as an X core font is tried through
fontconfig for matching, FreeType for rasterizing and the X RENDER
extension for compositing.
A family name such as
.Ql \&"DejaVu Sans\&" ,
which most systems have only as a scalable font, takes this path, and
uses fontconfig's own pattern syntax.
This is what gives real anti-aliasing and full UTF-8, neither of which
the core font path can provide.
.Pp
No field or prefix selects the backend: it is decided purely by whether
the string resolves as an X core font first.
A string resolving through neither falls back to
.Ql fixed ,
so one bad value never leaves text unrenderable.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/themes/
Where theme files live, at the first of the several locations
.Xr icowm 1
looks in.
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/themes/default.json
The theme shipped with
.Xr icowm 1 .
The same values are built into the binary, so a session with no theme
file still looks like this; the two differ only in the name they
report,
.Ql Default (built-in)
when the values come from the binary.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A theme that changes only its window colors, everything else keeping
the built-in default:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "name": "slate",
    "-author": "Jane Doe",

    "window": {
        "active": {
            "color": {
                "background": "#9AAEC8",
                "foreground": "#1B222E"
            },
            "font": "fixed bold"
        },
        "inactive": {
            "color": {
                "background": "#D0D9E5",
                "foreground": "#3A4351"
            },
            "font": "fixed"
        }
    }
}
.Ed
.Pp
A theme asking for a scalable font, which takes the fontconfig path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "name": "sans",
    "window": {
        "active": { "font": "DejaVu Sans:weight=bold:size=11" },
        "inactive": { "font": "DejaVu Sans:size=11" }
    }
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr icowm 1 ,
.Xr icowm-msg 1 ,
.Xr icowm 5 ,
.Xr icowm-a11y 5 ,
.Xr icowm-bindings 5 ,
.Xr icowm-memguard 5 ,
.Xr icowm-menu 5 ,
.Xr icowm-randr 5 ,
.Xr icowm-rules 5 ,
.Xr icowm-session 5
